00:27:44.128 --> 00:27:47.148
Thank you so much, Jackie, and for all the work that Save the Children does.

490
00:27:47.568 --> 00:27:51.468
I just wanted to ask you, from your experience dealing with children

491
00:27:51.528 --> 00:27:55.428
who this bill may apply to if it was a law, what

492
00:27:55.468 --> 00:27:58.808
are their stories? Why do they end up in this situation?

493
00:27:58.868 --> 00:27:59.988
What can you tell us about them?

494
00:28:01.168 --> 00:28:04.728
What we know from talking with our partners that work on the frontline is that a

495
00:28:04.828 --> 00:28:08.758
key driver of being homeless and being on the streets as

496
00:28:08.828 --> 00:28:12.408
a young person is through experiencing abuse and harm, and sadly,

497
00:28:12.888 --> 00:28:16.268
it can be in their own homes, and without the ability to deal with it.

498
00:28:16.968 --> 00:28:20.948
Harrowing stories by young people who had no place to go were shared at the

499
00:28:21.888 --> 00:28:25.488
final Child Poverty Monitor launch that was held at Waitematā

500
00:28:25.508 --> 00:28:28.647
in Auckland, I think around three years ago.

501
00:28:28.668 --> 00:28:31.168
And we need to be able to address those drivers.

502
00:28:31.207 --> 00:28:35.108
We cannot criminalize these young people who simply have nowhere to go.

503
00:28:35.148 --> 00:28:38.808
We also know that those frontline providers are struggling with funding

504
00:28:39.308 --> 00:28:41.548
and capability to address the need.

505
00:28:42.028 --> 00:28:45.628
And we know from people that reach out and community

506
00:28:45.708 --> 00:28:49.488
stories, and stories feels like the wrong word because it's their

507
00:28:50.228 --> 00:28:54.028
lives and it's their experiences, that the ability to afford

508
00:28:54.128 --> 00:28:57.798
private rental houses is very, very hard, and that is pushing

509
00:28:57.808 --> 00:29:01.748
regular ... well, families that we should be able to house, that are

510
00:29:01.848 --> 00:29:04.378
not beset by addiction and issues, into homelessness.

511
00:29:04.408 --> 00:29:08.388
So it's not limited to people who have addiction

512
00:29:08.528 --> 00:29:08.848
and

513
00:29:11.008 --> 00:29:14.628
those other sort of issues that we sort of see at the frontline of homelessness.

514
00:29:14.688 --> 00:29:18.028
It is increasingly people who really just cannot afford to make ends meet.

515
00:29:19.088 --> 00:29:19.388
Thank you.

516
00:29:20.268 --> 00:29:24.108
Thank you, Jackie. We don't have any further questions, so thank you very much

517
00:29:24.188 --> 00:29:25.708
for your submission.

518
00:29:25.788 --> 00:29:26.518
Thank you, Kelda.

519
00:29:27.128 --> 00:29:30.608
Thank you. Next is in person, Reverend Brett

520
00:29:31.148 --> 00:29:34.288
Reed and Leanne Munro. If they're here, thank you.

521
00:29:34.438 --> 00:29:35.208
Please come forward.

522
00:29:38.908 --> 00:29:41.128
Welcome. We've got you for 10 minutes.

523
00:29:41.188 --> 00:29:44.988
Your submission has been read, and if you want to just leave some

524
00:29:45.048 --> 00:29:46.328
time for some questions,

525
00:29:47.268 --> 00:29:48.597
we're in your hands. Thank you.

526
00:29:48.648 --> 00:29:52.168
Sure. Great. Tuhiia ki te rangi. Tuhiia ki te

527
00:29:52.248 --> 00:29:55.847
whenua. Tuhiia ki te ngākau o ngā tāngata

528
00:29:55.928 --> 00:29:59.348
katoa. Ko te mea nui, ko te

529
00:29:59.368 --> 00:29:59.928
aroha.

530
00:30:00.748 --> 00:30:04.288
E mihi ana ahau ki Te Atua. Nāna nei ngā mea katoa.

531
00:30:04.988 --> 00:30:08.228
E ngā Mema Pāremata, tēnā koutou katoa.

532
00:30:09.010 --> 00:30:10.720
Me nga kaiwhakapuoro hoki,

533
00:30:11.720 --> 00:30:15.600
tena koutou katoa. Greetings to you all, and thank you

534
00:30:15.660 --> 00:30:18.520
for this opportunity for us to present today.

535
00:30:19.220 --> 00:30:22.680
My name is Brett Reed. I'm the Minister of Ngaio Union Church, a

536
00:30:23.120 --> 00:30:26.819
church in Wellington. I'm joined by the Reverend Leanne Munro,

537
00:30:27.080 --> 00:30:30.780
a member of our congregation, and we're presenting this submission on

538
00:30:30.820 --> 00:30:32.720
behalf of Ngaio Union Church.

539
00:30:33.980 --> 00:30:37.820
As a faith community committed to the way of Jesus, we are guided

540
00:30:37.920 --> 00:30:40.100
by the values of compassion,

541
00:30:41.660 --> 00:30:45.300
love of neighbor, and care for those in need.

542
00:30:46.540 --> 00:30:50.100
It is because of these values that we oppose the

543
00:30:50.120 --> 00:30:51.900
proposed move on orders.

544
00:30:54.320 --> 00:30:58.080
We all want safe and welcoming public spaces,

545
00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:02.920
but homelessness is not solved by moving people

546
00:31:03.080 --> 00:31:04.720
