547
00:31:05.680 --> 00:31:09.540
The proposed measures simply displace people from places

548
00:31:09.620 --> 00:31:11.410
and communities they rely on,

549
00:31:12.260 --> 00:31:15.920
while leaving the underlying need for housing and support

550
00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:16.760
unchanged.

551
00:31:17.880 --> 00:31:21.840
In many cases, simply moving people on will make

552
00:31:21.900 --> 00:31:25.300
it even harder for them to access the help they need.

553
00:31:27.200 --> 00:31:31.180
Over the past week and a bit, you've heard from experts in the field,

554
00:31:31.280 --> 00:31:34.160
and we tautoko what they have already said.

555
00:31:35.980 --> 00:31:39.580
In our written submission, we speak about a longtime association with

556
00:31:39.640 --> 00:31:41.060
DCM in Wellington.

557
00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:45.980
Through their work, we know that the claim that rough sleepers

558
00:31:46.020 --> 00:31:49.910
have somewhere to move on to is simply untrue,

559
00:31:50.820 --> 00:31:53.480
and Murray Edridge touched on this as well.

560
00:31:54.640 --> 00:31:58.360
In the last quarter alone, DCM supported 150 people with no

561
00:31:58.420 --> 00:32:02.380
house or shelter to go to, and they continue to support dozens

562
00:32:02.460 --> 00:32:06.380
of people sleeping rough because there is nowhere else

563
00:32:06.440 --> 00:32:07.680
for them to live.

564
00:32:09.900 --> 00:32:13.880
Homelessness is a complex issue with housing, health,

565
00:32:13.940 --> 00:32:15.180
and social causes.

566
00:32:16.100 --> 00:32:19.900
The people affected are often living with poverty, mental ill

567
00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:23.400
health, addiction, or multiple challenges at once.

568
00:32:24.480 --> 00:32:27.320
These are issues that require coordinated,

569
00:32:27.880 --> 00:32:29.480
evidence-based support,

570
00:32:30.360 --> 00:32:33.900
not punitive measures. And I'll hand over to

571
00:32:33.940 --> 00:32:34.380
Leanne.

572
00:32:35.480 --> 00:32:39.340
Tena koutou katoa. I'm speaking as a person who somewhat

573
00:32:39.360 --> 00:32:42.240
imperfectly tries to live out her faith every day.

574
00:32:43.089 --> 00:32:46.100
The biblical gospels of Matthew, Mark, and Luke each tell of an

575
00:32:46.140 --> 00:32:50.040
occasion where Jesus of Nazareth was engaged in conversation

576
00:32:50.080 --> 00:32:51.680
and asked a simple question,

577
00:32:52.730 --> 00:32:54.140
"Which command is the greatest?"

578
00:32:55.880 --> 00:32:59.589
His response is taken directly from the Hebrew scriptures he knew, the Torah.

579
00:33:00.450 --> 00:33:04.180
"Love God with all your heart, soul, mind, and strength, and love your neighbor as

580
00:33:04.220 --> 00:33:05.260
you love yourself."

581
00:33:06.360 --> 00:33:10.260
In the Gospel of Luke, in response to a further, some

582
00:33:10.300 --> 00:33:13.580
would say, smartarsed question, but the jury is out on that,

583
00:33:14.380 --> 00:33:16.580
he is asked, "But who is my neighbor?"

584
00:33:17.440 --> 00:33:21.369
And he responds with a story that many of us have come to know as the

585
00:33:21.480 --> 00:33:22.720
story of the Good Samaritan.

586
00:33:23.960 --> 00:33:27.500
In effect, Jesus says, "Your neighbor is the one

587
00:33:27.960 --> 00:33:30.480
you see as different to yourself,

588
00:33:31.380 --> 00:33:32.490
and not in a good way."

589
00:33:34.120 --> 00:33:37.830
Last year, walking down Willis Street to the bank, I noticed two different people

590
00:33:37.860 --> 00:33:41.560
in separate locations sitting on the pavement outside the

591
00:33:41.600 --> 00:33:42.180
buildings.

592
00:33:43.060 --> 00:33:46.460
Each had a card seeking help from passersby.

593
00:33:47.260 --> 00:33:50.380
I didn't stop. I was in a hurry to get to my meeting.

594
00:33:52.000 --> 00:33:55.410
Afterwards, though, I approached the woman and greeted her, receiving a very

595
00:33:55.520 --> 00:33:59.280
gracious response, and said I was going to get a cuppa and would she

596
00:33:59.340 --> 00:34:03.190
like one. It was one of Wellington's lovely sunny but slightly

597
00:34:03.320 --> 00:34:04.140
cool days.

598
00:34:06.660 --> 00:34:10.281
She was surprised but thanked me and said yes, and on my

599
00:34:10.321 --> 00:34:14.301
return, when I offered her a piece of banana loaf I'd also purchased,

600
00:34:14.960 --> 00:34:18.680
she declined graciously, saying the cup of

601
00:34:18.781 --> 00:34:20.220
tea was enough,

602
00:34:21.281 --> 00:34:23.301
and I felt incredibly humbled.

603
00:34:23.801 --> 00:34:24.060
Mm.

604
00:34:25.120 --> 00:34:29.080
We talked for another minute or so, and I asked if she knew about DCM

605
00:34:29.120 --> 00:34:32.660
and the City Mission, and she replied yes, and then we said

606
00:34:32.700 --> 00:34:34.720
goodbye and she wished me a good day.

607
00:34:35.580 --> 00:34:39.560
Further up the road, a youngish man I'd seen appeared to be talking to

608
00:34:39.580 --> 00:34:40.361
himself.

609
00:34:41.240 --> 00:34:45.160
Somewhat in trepidation, I approached him and greeted

610
00:34:45.180 --> 00:34:49.040
him, saying my name, getting an enthusiastic, "Kia ora," in

611
00:34:49.080 --> 00:34:49.720
response.

612
00:34:51.440 --> 00:34:55.321
I offered him the piece of loaf, to which he replied, "Oh, are you sure, ma'am?"

613
00:34:55.761 --> 00:34:59.690
Now, I may be nearly 64, and I may have silver hair, but I'm still not used

614
00:34:59.720 --> 00:35:00.630
to being called ma'am.

615
00:35:02.720 --> 00:35:06.640
As we parted company, he also graciously wished

616
00:35:06.700 --> 00:35:07.980
me a good day.

617
00:35:09.560 --> 00:35:13.180
I was struck by their dignity, their cautious friendliness,

618
00:35:13.800 --> 00:35:15.840
and the graciousness of their responses.

619
00:35:16.640 --> 00:35:20.220
I was also aware as I spoke with them of the

620
00:35:20.320 --> 00:35:24.240
sidelong looks we got from our fellow Wellingtonians who continued

621
00:35:24.300 --> 00:35:25.230
to pass by,

622
00:35:26.180 --> 00:35:28.580
as if it was odd for two people to share

623
00:35:28.620 --> 00:35:31.480
conversation on a public street.

624
00:35:32.580 --> 00:35:35.900
And I felt a sense of shame that these two

625
00:35:36.580 --> 00:35:37.920
fellow Wellingtonians

626
00:35:39.260 --> 00:35:41.860
were having to do this, for whatever reason.

627
00:35:43.660 --> 00:35:46.070
There is no simple solution

628
00:35:46.920 --> 00:35:50.880
to the homelessness, the rough sleeping, the begging that

629
00:35:50.940 --> 00:35:51.640
we see.

630
00:35:53.860 --> 00:35:57.400
But it appears that this is what this proposed law change

631
00:35:57.720 --> 00:35:58.800
seeks to be.

632
00:36:00.340 --> 00:36:04.180
But we are talking about fellow human beings, people

633
00:36:04.300 --> 00:36:05.840
like you and I,

634
00:36:07.140 --> 00:36:08.660
who are different perhaps,

635
00:36:09.460 --> 00:36:13.020
and who for a variety of reasons have ended up where they are

636
00:36:14.716 --> 00:36:18.156
Because I am commanded to love my

637
00:36:18.216 --> 00:36:20.376
neighbor as myself,

638
00:36:21.596 --> 00:36:24.496
I can do no other than oppose this proposed law

639
00:36:24.556 --> 00:36:27.896
change and ask that you, as our elected

640
00:36:27.936 --> 00:36:31.376
representatives, show mercy and compassion

641
00:36:31.856 --> 00:36:35.836
to those that this law, perhaps unintentionally, I hope

642
00:36:35.976 --> 00:36:36.216
so,

643
00:36:37.176 --> 00:36:40.236
seeks to put out of sight, out of mind.

644
00:36:43.156 --> 00:36:46.956
Instead of move on orders, we urge the government to invest in what we

645
00:36:46.975 --> 00:36:50.236
know works. More social and affordable housing,

646
00:36:51.096 --> 00:36:54.996
stronger health and addiction services, and outreach programs.

647
00:36:57.216 --> 00:37:00.985
Justice is not about punishing people for having

648
00:37:01.036 --> 00:37:01.996
nowhere to go.

649
00:37:02.976 --> 00:37:06.416
It's about restoring dignity, providing support,

650
00:37:07.176 --> 00:37:09.736
and addressing the causes of homelessness.

651
00:37:10.776 --> 00:37:14.476
For these reasons, we urge you to reject the proposed

652
00:37:14.516 --> 00:37:18.316
legislation and invest instead in evidence-based

653
00:37:18.516 --> 00:37:21.396
responses that we know work.

654
00:37:21.996 --> 00:37:25.526
Thank you very much, Brett and

655
00:37:25.576 --> 00:37:27.736
Leanne. A very heartfelt submission.

