4979
05:47:03.724 --> 05:47:07.484
on. Over the past year, we've supported on average 10

4980
05:47:07.544 --> 05:47:09.194
people a night through our shelter.

4981
05:47:09.584 --> 05:47:13.144
We've provided over 7,000 meals. We've helped

4982
05:47:13.344 --> 05:47:17.264
15 people move into housing and reconnect with whānau.

4983
05:47:17.324 --> 05:47:20.374
We've achieved this through an incredible network of volunteers, community

4984
05:47:20.464 --> 05:47:24.434
organization, health providers, police, and local supporters.

4985
05:47:24.784 --> 05:47:28.314
As governors, we're responsible and accountable for the

4986
05:47:28.404 --> 05:47:29.003
outcomes.

4987
05:47:29.844 --> 05:47:33.464
When we look back over the last year, we measure our success by not how many people

4988
05:47:33.504 --> 05:47:37.354
we've accommodated overnight, but the measure of success by people that we've

4989
05:47:37.384 --> 05:47:41.334
moved into housing to reconnect with whānau, to engage with health services,

4990
05:47:41.724 --> 05:47:44.324
and to start to begin to rebuild their lives.

4991
05:47:45.194 --> 05:47:47.904
Those are the outcomes that strengthen communities.

4992
05:47:48.384 --> 05:47:52.364
These outcomes tell us that homelessness isn't simply a policing issue.

4993
05:47:53.144 --> 05:47:56.604
It's a housing issue, it's a health issue, and it's a social issue.

4994
05:47:58.424 --> 05:48:02.344
When people are offered safety, dignity, support instead

4995
05:48:02.404 --> 05:48:06.164
of simply being displaced, they engage, they accept

4996
05:48:06.184 --> 05:48:09.784
help, they reconnect with services, and they begin to move

4997
05:48:09.844 --> 05:48:13.724
towards stable housing. This is exactly what we've seen at Kim's

4998
05:48:13.804 --> 05:48:17.644
Way. One of the strongest partnerships that we've developed over the last 12

4999
05:48:17.684 --> 05:48:21.464
months is with our local police. We often encounter, when the

5000
